                 VERSION 1 REVISION 46 -- BUILT ON 11 Oct 93
              *************************************************

Add support for accepting rlogin connections as well as the telnet
connections that telnetd.device has previously known about.

To get telnetd.device to watch a port number in rlogind mode, specify the
'RLOGIND' keyword in the configuration file.  The standard rlogind port is
513, so the line

	513 5 255.255.255.255 rlogind

would allocate five units on the standard rlogind port to accept rlogin
connections.

NOTE: THE DEMO VERSION IS NOT CAPABLE OF ACCEPTING RLOGIN CONNECTIONS!

Modified the makefile to build 68000 and 68020 versions of the device.

              *************************************************
                 VERSION 1 REVISION 57 -- BUILT ON 27 Dec 93
              *************************************************

The telnet mode will now time out after five seconds if no TELOPT_ECHO
response is seen.  This allows (*seriously*) broken telnet clients (that
can't really be called telnet clients at all) to connect to the device.
Previous versions would wait indefinately (or until the connection was
closed by the other side) for the TELOPT_ECHO negotiation to be acked.

              *************************************************
                 VERSION 1 REVISION 65 -- BUILT ON 19 Jan 94
              *************************************************

telnetd.device now supports the ATH modem command.   It is primarily
intended to allow BBS programs to mark a unit as in-use.  Thus, if the
system does a local login on a port, the BBS can send ATH1 to take the unit
off-line.  Incoming connections will then automatically roll over to the
next available unit.

